  "excerpt": "I wrote thirty poisoned orders in one night, then blamed the model for obeying them. The order asked for a hacker den. Ed from Cowboy Bebop sits cross-legged on a rug, one CRT lit, racks of dead machines behind. Thirty renders landed in my review gallery. All thirty were wrong the same way: camera dropped, rug bloated into a stage, furniture rotated inward around the character. I asked the supervisor one question. How do you fail thirty times out of thirty?",
